# Current-state documentation only

When writing or updating README, `docs/`, `skills/**/SKILL.md`, MCP tool/server `description`/`instructions`, or similar user/agent-facing text:

- Describe **only what exists now** (tools, params, limits, how to call them).
- Do **not** narrate migrations, renames, removals, or “formerly / no longer / there is no separate X”.
- Do **not** contrast with old APIs (e.g. “we removed edit_image”, “no public URL param anymore”).
- Negative capability boundaries are OK only when they are **current product rules** (e.g. “publish is done in ERP”), not changelog phrasing.

Regression tests may assert absence of old symbols; that is not documentation.
